{
  "title": "Recipe card checkbox glyphs leak into ingredient text",
  "description": "Some recipe-card ingredient lines are being captured with UI \
checkbox glyphs still attached, leaving both `raw` and `item` values dirty \
even though the source HTML contains clean ingredient text in structured \
recipe markup.\n\
\n\
Concrete example from \
`data/pipeline-snapshots/halfbakedharvest-com_easy-cheesy-eggs.json`, \
cross-checked against cached HTML at \
`~/.ramekin/http-cache/halfbakedharvest-com_easy-cheesy-eggs/response.bin`:\n\
\n\
The source page includes clean recipe data such as:\n\
`\"recipeIngredient\":[\"1 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil\", \"2 \
tablespoons salted butter\", \"1 clove garlic, chopped\", ...]`\n\
\n\
But the snapshot produces ingredient rows like:\n\
`raw: \"▢ 1 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil\"`\n\
`item: \"▢ 1 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil\"`\n\
`raw: \"▢ 2 tablespoons salted butter\"`\n\
`item: \"▢ 2 tablespoons salted butter\"`\n\
\n\
Expected behavior: strip recipe-card checkbox UI glyphs before parsing so the \
ingredient text matches the recipe content. The current output leaves obvious \
presentation junk in the parsed ingredient fields.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "ingredient-parser",
  ],
